-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- knowledge-service.http  (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
-- Place in project root — Run requests with the green arrow
-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081/api/v1

### Create a note
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

 {
   "title": "Kafka Consumer Groups",
   "content": "A consumer group allows multiple consumers to share a topic.",
   "category": "kafka",
  "tags": ["kafka", "messaging"]
 }

### Get all notes
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes

### Get note by ID  (paste a real ID after running create)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/PASTE-ID-HERE

### Get by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/category/kafka

### Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/search?q=consumer&page=0&size=5

### Update a note
PUT {{baseUrl}}/notes/PASTE-ID-HERE
Content-Type: application/json

 {
  "title": "Kafka Consumer Groups — updated",
   "content": "Updated content here.",
 "category": "kafka",
   "tags": ["kafka", "messaging", "updated"]
 }

### Delete a note
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/notes/PASTE-ID-HERE

### Health check
GET http://localhost:8081/actuator/health

 ── Validation error test ─────────────────────────────
### Should return 400 — title is blank
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json

 {
   "title": "",
   "content": "Some content"
 }

### Should return 404 — ID does not exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/non-existent-id